what is delta lake?
A: Delta lake is an open source storage layer that sits on top of your existing data lake( like s3 or adls) and adds reliability 
and performance to it. It addresses the key weakness of traditional data lakes by providing
ACID Transactions - so concurrent reads/writes are safe
Time travel - query data as it existed at any point in the past using versioning
schema enforcement and evolution - prevents bad data from corrupting your tables
support for dml operations like (MERGE, UPDATE AND DELETE)
A transction log(_delta_log) that tracks every change made to the table.
** Delta lake stores data as parquet files with a transaction log
The secret sauce - a JSON based log that tracks every change 
same table can handle both batch and streaming data.


Apache spark lacks the ACID transaction capabilities So using delta lake we can overcome that issue

	1) Delta Lake అనే పదాన్ని storage layer అనే విధంగా వాడతారు, కానీ దీనిని storage system అనీ కాదు.
	2) Delta Lake అనేది నేరుగా డేటాను స్టోర్ చేయదు. దానికి తన సొంత స్టోరేజ్ వ్యవస్థ ఉండదు.
	3) ఇది క్లౌడ్ object storage (ఉదాహరణకి Azure Blob Storage, AWS S3, Google Cloud Storage) పైన కూర్చుంది.అంటే, మీ డేటా ఈ cloud storage లో ఉంది, కాని Delta Lake దానిపైన ACID transaction, time travel, transaction logs, schema control, version tracking వంటివి కలిపి దీన్ని visibly organized and reliable data tables గా మార్చుతుంది.
	4) Delta Lake అనేది cloud storage లో ఉన్న raw files ను structured & trustworthy format లో represent చేయడానికి ఉపయోగపడే ఒక storage layer. కానీ, cloud storage లాంటి physical storage అదే కాకపోతుంది.
	5) Delta Lake అనేది Apache Parquet ఫైళ్లపై నిర్మించబడిన storage format.
	
	Delta Lake యొక్క ముఖ్య ఉద్దేశ్యం
	Raw data lakes లో ఉన్న inconsistent data ను clean చేసి, trustworthy data గా మార్చడం.
	Real-time & batch processing రెండింటికీ support చేయడం.
	Data warehouse లాంటి performance ను data lake లోనే అందించడం.
	Machine Learning, BI, Analytics కోసం data ను prepare చేయడం.
	
	Delta Lake ఎలా పని చేస్తుంది?
	a) Parquet Files: Data ను columnar format లో store చేస్తుంది.
	b) Transaction Log: ప్రతి write/update/delete ను track చేసే JSON/Parquet logs ను maintain చేస్తుంది.
	c) ACID Transactions: Partial writes, corrupt data లాంటి issues లేకుండా safe updates చేస్తుంది.
	d) Schema Enforcement & Evolution: Schema mismatch ఉన్న data reject చేయడం లేదా adapt చేయడం.
	e) Time Travel: గత versions ను query చేయడం, rollback చేయడం.

2) Databricks Architecture splits into two parts
Control plane and Data plane
control plane - owned by databricks (Lives in own databricks cloud account)
Data plane - owned by customer (Your cloud account aws/gcp/azure)

Control plane - Think of like control plane is like brain/Manager of databricks
what lives in Control plane?
Databricks webui - the notebook or sql query or etc interfaces we use daily.
cluster manager - decides when to start/stop the clusters
job scheduler - schedules and triggers your pipelines/jobs
unity catalog metastore - stores table definations, permissions(not actual data)
MLflow tracking server - tracks ML experiments
Workflow Orchestration - manages DAGS and dependencies.
KEY POINT : Your actual data NEVER enters the control plane. only metadata, logs and configurations live here.


Data plane - Think of the data plane like the actual data
what lives in data plane?
	- Apache spark clusters (VMs in your cloud account)
	- DBFS (Databricks file system)
	- Your actual data (S3, ADLS, GCS)
	- Delta lake tables
	- Runtime executuion Enviornment

How they talk each other?
You (Browser) 
|
control plane (Databricks cloud)
	- Autheticates you
	- Sends instructions to Data Plane
|
Data Plane (Your cloud account)
	- spins up spark clusters
	- Reads/writes your actual data
	- Sends results back to control plane UI


