❌ Real Problems with Plain Data Lake + Spark
Problem 1 — No ACID Transactions
Pipeline A writing data to S3  ──┐
                                  ├→ SAME TABLE → Data Corruption!
Pipeline B writing data to S3  ──┘

Example: Two ETL jobs running parallel
→ Job A writes 1 lakh records
→ Job B writes 50k records simultaneously
→ Result = Mixed/corrupted data
→ Nobody knows which records are valid!

Problem 2 — No Update or Delete
Imagine a customer calls and says "Delete my personal data" (GDPR Request)
In plain Data Lake — nearly IMPOSSIBLE
Parquet files are immutable — you cant update a single row
Only option = rewrite ENTIRE dataset = very expensive!

Problem 3 — Failed Jobs Leave Dirty Data
ETL Job starts writing 10 lakh records...
   Written 6 lakh records...
   JOB CRASHES! ❌
 Result in Data Lake:
→ 6 lakh records written (incomplete!)
→ No rollback possible
→ Downstream pipelines read WRONG data
→ Reports show WRONG numbers!
Problem 4 — No Schema Enforcement
Day 1: { "name": "Ravi", "salary": 50000 }       ✅
Day 2: { "name": "Kumar", "salary": "fifty thousand" } ✅ (lake accepts it!)
Day 3: { "name": 12345, "salary": null }           ✅ (lake accepts this too!)

Result → Your salary column has integers, strings, nulls mixed!
→ Spark job crashes or gives wrong aggregations
Problem 5 — No Time Travel
Monday: Table had 1 lakh records — Pipeline ran fine ✅
Tuesday: Someone accidentally deleted 20k records ❌
Wednesday: You realize reports are wrong!

Question: What was the data on Monday?
Answer in plain Data Lake: NO WAY TO KNOW! 😱
→ Data is gone forever
Problem 6 — Small File Problem
Streaming pipeline writes data every 1 minute
→ After 1 day = 1440 small files
→ After 1 month = 43,200 small files
→ Spark reads each file separately
→ Query performance becomes very SLOW
→ Even simple COUNT(*) takes 10+ minutes!
Problem 7 — No Audit Trail
Who changed this data?
When was it changed?
What was the old value?

Plain Data Lake answer: NO IDEA! 🤷
→ Compliance teams go crazy
→ Debugging data issues = impossible
